[{:db/id 17592186059690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a1135e70-c8a0-50ee-ba8b-a60797a22c04"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a1135e70-c8a0-50ee-ba8b-a60797a22c04" :question/id #uuid "a1135e70-c8a0-50ee-ba8b-a60797a22c04" :question/math-academy-id "q-1477" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(P⇒Q).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(P⇒Q)≡¬(¬P∨Q).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬P∨Q)≡¬(¬P)∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nFinally, canceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬P)∧¬Q≡P∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P∧¬Q.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0b770ae3-a6bf-565c-b1f8-035f0cda7d32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0b770ae3-a6bf-565c-b1f8-035f0cda7d32" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b770ae3-a6bf-565c-b1f8-035f0cda7d32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6fc52a1a-3940-5732-a868-a532984c3e32" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fc52a1a-3940-5732-a868-a532984c3e32" "answer-baf71b07-e263-5232-88b3-0e6cfa44ae4e" "answer-8bd4cd09-8cbb-5ab2-9eee-c2ef187bad59" "answer-9bcc4291-0a68-5242-920b-da5bf575f0b1" "answer-ec239135-a191-53fd-ab45-832fc11ac4d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fc52a1a-3940-5732-a868-a532984c3e32" :answer/id #uuid "6fc52a1a-3940-5732-a868-a532984c3e32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baf71b07-e263-5232-88b3-0e6cfa44ae4e" :answer/id #uuid "baf71b07-e263-5232-88b3-0e6cfa44ae4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∨¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bd4cd09-8cbb-5ab2-9eee-c2ef187bad59" :answer/id #uuid "8bd4cd09-8cbb-5ab2-9eee-c2ef187bad59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q∨P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bcc4291-0a68-5242-920b-da5bf575f0b1" :answer/id #uuid "9bcc4291-0a68-5242-920b-da5bf575f0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q∨¬P" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec239135-a191-53fd-ab45-832fc11ac4d9" :answer/id #uuid "ec239135-a191-53fd-ab45-832fc11ac4d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∧¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060149 :question/problem "$\\,$ Pay the bill, or your power will be shut off.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ Pay the bill.\n\n- $B:$ Your power will be shut off.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A∨B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬A⇒B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You don't pay the bill.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ If you don't pay the bill, then your power will be shut off." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186057277 :answer-field/correct 17592186057279 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fdb480fb-7595-51de-b205-79626369178f" :activity/id #uuid "fdb480fb-7595-51de-b205-79626369178f" :activity/title "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049805 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-fa95311a-452f-53c8-b4cc-be5bc9963eec" "step-d47622de-c52c-55f3-b089-ee15881a00d2" "step-8b066a8e-899d-55a1-8411-df8d5e53b232" "step-c7860837-e731-5c21-a8c2-238981203349" "step-b746c91b-d837-5aea-9df8-0783cb162ef2"] :activity/first-step "step-fa95311a-452f-53c8-b4cc-be5bc9963eec" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fa95311a-452f-53c8-b4cc-be5bc9963eec" :step/id #uuid "fa95311a-452f-53c8-b4cc-be5bc9963eec" :step/content "question-a1135e70-c8a0-50ee-ba8b-a60797a22c04" :step/next "step-d47622de-c52c-55f3-b089-ee15